.TH FREOPEN 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
freopen \- reopen a Crunch stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.B FILE *freopen(const char *path, const char *mode, FILE *stream);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Replaces the file associated with a stream, preserving the stream pointer
and descriptor number. Modes are as for
.BR fopen (3crunch).
When path is NULL, Crunch reopens the existing file through /proc/self/fd;
this requires a mounted, accessible procfs and can fail for some descriptors.
Streams are unbuffered. On failure the original stream is closed and must
not be used; standard stream objects remain allocated but have no descriptor.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the original stream on success, or NULL with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fopen (3crunch),
.BR fclose (3crunch),
.BR freopen (3)
